od we just  extract the maximum value of the block  so how do we do it in Python the easiest  way is to import Pi extremes a python  package that deals with extreme value  analysis uh you should also import  pandas because Pi extremes while being  built on scikit-learn is takes a pandas  series as its input  and then you read the time series for  example here the water levels at battery  Station in New York uh which helps  monitor and prevent flooding in New York  uh and then  you create your model it's the pi  extremes.eda  and again you initialize it with the  time series that we just read  and then you run get extremes  you specify the method in this case it's  the block maximum method the method  we've been discussing there are other  methods which we might get to if I have  some time at the end  and we specify the block size which is  365 and the quarter days colloquially  known as a year  and  then  we just  ask for example to plot extremes and we  get this beautiful graph that  immediately tells us which data points  are to be used  down the line in the extreme value  analysis which is obviously the highest  point of each year but this gives a good  visualization it can also immediately  show us that there are some gaps in our  data  we might be missing some extreme events  within those gaps and we need to be  mindful of that uh if the gaps were very  large we'd probably want to invalidate  those years where there's a large gap  but if the gaps are small then we can  assume that no maximum event appeared  within those gaps  all right after we did that we just hit  a model we fit a gev distribution to the  extremes by running the fit model method  of the model object  and now we want to sample the  distribution at specific  cumulative probabilities so we use the  cumulative probability function  and in the pi experience package we use  it we do it using the get summary method  and for example here I requested the  1050 100 and 500 year  uh return values so eve